Senior FinOps Engineer / Cloud Cost Optimization Lead (Hybrid)
Location: Dallas, TX
Duration: 12 Months

Interview: Virtual / In-Person
Work Arrangement: Hybrid – 4 Days Onsite
Note: Dallas, TX local candidates required.

Job Description
We are seeking a Senior FinOps Engineer / Cloud Cost Optimization Lead to drive AWS cloud cost optimization initiatives and establish a sustainable FinOps practice within the Data Platforms group.
The ideal candidate will have strong hands-on AWS infrastructure engineering experience, expertise in cloud cost management, and a proven ability to deliver measurable cost savings through automation, monitoring, and infrastructure optimization.

Key Responsibilities
Analyze AWS spending and identify opportunities for cost reduction.
Optimize AWS infrastructure and data platform services.
Implement automated cost monitoring, anomaly detection, and remediation.
Establish FinOps governance, budgeting, forecasting, and reporting.
Integrate cost optimization practices into Terraform, CI/CD, and infrastructure workflows.
Collaborate with engineering and finance teams to track savings and improve cost efficiency.

Required Skills & Experience
8+ years of cloud infrastructure or financial management experience.
4+ years of hands-on AWS cost optimization experience at scale.
Strong expertise in AWS Cost Explorer, CUR, Compute Optimizer, Budgets, Savings Plans, Reserved Instances, and AWS Organizations.
Experience optimizing AWS EMR, EC2, Glue, Athena, and S3.
Strong Python, SQL, and Terraform skills.
Experience with multi-account AWS environments and multi-million-dollar cloud spending.
Proven track record of delivering measurable cost savings and implementing continuous FinOps practices.

Nice to Have
FinOps or AWS Professional certifications.
Experience with CloudHealth, Cloudability, CloudZero, or Kubecost.
Knowledge of AWS EDP/private pricing negotiations.
Experience with Snowflake, Databricks, or multi-cloud environments.
Finance/FP&A collaboration experience.

